ld_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n**Tested versions**\nReproducible in: 4.6 Beta 3\nNot reproducible in: 4.5.1 Stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.beta3 - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4080 SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7247) - AMD Ryzen 9 9950X 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 125.6 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nDiffuse shading appears broken and inconsistent and producing artifacts near the pole of the sphere oriented toward the sky.\nInitially I suspected a normals or pinching issue, but the mesh looks fine. HDRI is also clean and behaves as expected.\nI’m running out of obvious suspects for where this could be coming from.\n\n<img width=\"895\" height=\"685\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0c903f75-dd79-458e-952f-19048e8ee30a\" />\n<img width=\"885\" height=\"687\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4ba587ab-573a-4a0d-a0e7-13717714a61d\" />\n<img width=\"875\" height=\"684\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e6a25151-11c3-49ce-adbe-a6e982fd0e71\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- New scene\n\n- New WorldEnvironment PanoramaSky (ProceduralSky seems ok)\n\n- Add HDRi image - in my case **https://polyhaven.com/a/kloofendal_48d_partly_cloudy_puresky** But custom sky shader produced issue as well\n- Add mesh, sphere\n- Add Standard material, red albedo, roughness to 1\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[Diffuse-bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24500610/Diffuse-bug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github